# Copy to .env and set your PC's LAN IP (same as shown in Expo QR / ipconfig).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.137:3000/api
#
# iPhone on same Wi‑Fi: use `npm start` or `npm run start:lan` (no tunnel).
# If iOS says the Internet is offline / requests fail:
#   - Settings → Expo Go → Local Network → ON (or Privacy & Security → Local Network → Expo Go).
#   - PC firewall: allow Node (or port 3000) on Private networks.
#   - Phone and PC must be on the same Wi‑Fi (not guest / isolated AP).
#
# Tunnel (`npm run start:tunnel`): you still need EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL with your PC LAN IP — tunnel
# only carries Metro, not your Nest API on :3000.
# If you see ngrok errors like "remote gone away", use LAN (`npm start`) or check https://status.ngrok.com/
